<article class="env-remark" id="08ML">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08ML">Remark <span data-tag="08ML">91.10.10</span>.</a> Let $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed topos. We define a sequence of morphisms of first order thickenings </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_1), \mathcal{O}'_1) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_2), \mathcal{O}'_2) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_3), \mathcal{O}'_3)  \]
</div>
  <p> of $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O})$ to be a <em>complex</em> if the corresponding maps between the ideal sheaves $\mathcal{I}_ i$ give a complex of $\mathcal{O}$-modules $\mathcal{I}_3 \to \mathcal{I}_2 \to \mathcal{I}_1$ (i.e., the composition is zero). In this case the composition $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_1), \mathcal{O}'_1) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_3), \mathcal{O}'_3)$ factors through $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_3), \mathcal{O}'_3)$, i.e., the first order thickening $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_1), \mathcal{O}'_1)$ of $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O})$ is trivial and comes with a canonical trivialization $\pi : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_1), \mathcal{O}'_1) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O})$. </p>
  <p>We say a sequence of morphisms of first order thickenings </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_1), \mathcal{O}'_1) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_2), \mathcal{O}'_2) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}_3), \mathcal{O}'_3)  \]
</div>
  <p> of $(\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O})$ is <em>a short exact sequence</em> if the corresponding maps between ideal sheaves is a short exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{I}_3 \to \mathcal{I}_2 \to \mathcal{I}_1 \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. </p>
</article>